# P1: the device profile of c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate AT EIGHT USERS, copying the tp4-profile2-jobs conventions: status, an all-four reset and two gate arms on the SAME eight real-text coding
# prompts (8 x 4,096 tokens; user 0 asks 256 tokens out, the others 128, all ignore_eos; an eight-seat profile gets eight users, a four-seat profile still four: ops_profile_plan.plan_users): ops-twin
# unprofiled (the per-round trace_ms, the [PACKED-*] and [PHASE] splits and the texts), ops-trace profiled (tracy, op-support 20000 - 200000 segfaults the dispatch thread, any other count is refused - the CPP
# post-process only, a read-back after every 2nd verify replay, no prefill flush). One container gives 8-live rounds (two 64-row blocks), then the live count falls as users finish.
# NEVER CANCEL this job once the gate step has started: the profiler writes as root and a cancel can leave root-owned files that break the next checkout. A segfault in
# read_core_data_from_completion_queue is INFRA: do not raise op-support. Disk: the profile tree up to 4 GB; the guard stops the arm at 4 GB or 85% disk. NEVER delete the P8 base image.
# READ: ops-trace texts equal ops-twin's; the per-op table of one 64-row block's verify (the analysis picks the 4-user block trace; both blocks run the same one) against the four-seat best-ship profile,
# the per-live-count table (the marginal cost of a live user), the quad draft's share, and what the two blocks cost together. Duration (estimate): 150 min (100 best, 210 worst). Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/262k8 eight-seat 262k development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/262k8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/262k8 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate
C2_GATE_PLAN=ops-twin,ops-trace
C2_GATE_JIT=record
